From da023146d91a5eff4d5544d0439e6822aaa708b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:51:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Propagate V8 Windows registry linkage to Rust consumers

The Windows GNU V8 test link in run 38747669404 fails on RegOpenKeyEx, RegQueryValueEx and other registry imports: the C++ archive requires advapi32, but build.rs only emits winmm and dbghelp. Patch its actual metadata producer. The same omission remains in latest stable rusty_v8 152.2.0.

Regression: expose only the existing compiled build script, run its supported DENO_TRYBUILD mode for four Windows triples and Linux/macOS controls, and require each Windows dependency exactly once. This does not compile or download a V8 archive. Red: v8-link-metadata-red.log exit 3, Windows advapi32 absent. Green: v8-link-metadata-gates.log exit 0, test plus just fmt-check and just bazel-lock-check pass. Full native Windows linking remains a hosted acceptance gate.
